  {
   "id": 27,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1020,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 26,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 14 - Advanced latent persistence and sampler control\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: a reference picture and a prompt (stage A); the saved latent (stage B).\n\n**Controls**: Sigma Shift (Ratio Locked) sets the video / audio noise shift together (12 / 3 = core's H3 default); Sigma Inspector prints the schedule; First-Block Cache (bypassed) skips repeated block work. Stage A samples and SAVES the joint latent (Motion Context Save Latent). Stage B (muted, Ctrl+M to enable; mute stage A) loads it, and Merge AV writes noise masks: picture 0 (kept exactly), sound 1 (regenerated) - a new soundtrack for an existing clip without touching its picture.\n\n**Output**: stage A: the clip (MP4) + its latent on disk; stage B: the new sound (FLAC).\n\n**Limits**: a saved latent only fits the same size / length; Merge AV can also take picture from one latent and sound from another (video_mix / audio_mix).\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# 14 - Advanced latent persistence and sampler control\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: a reference picture and a prompt (stage A); the saved latent (stage B).\n\n**Controls**: Sigma Shift (Ratio Locked) sets the video / audio noise shift together (12 / 3 = core's H3 default); Sigma Inspector prints the schedule; First-Block Cache (bypassed) skips repeated block work. Stage A samples and SAVES the joint latent (Motion Context Save Latent). Stage B (muted, Ctrl+M to enable; mute stage A) loads it, and Merge AV writes noise masks: picture 0 (kept exactly), sound 1 (regenerated) - a new soundtrack for an existing clip without touching its picture.\n\n**Output**: stage A: the clip (MP4) + its latent on disk; stage B: the new sound (FLAC).\n\n**Limits**: a saved latent only fits the same size / length; Merge AV can also take picture from one latent and sound from another (video_mix / audio_mix).\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
